## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates understanding of AWS-native DevOps practices applied to SAP ABAP environments, requiring knowledge of both AWS supply chain security principles and SAP transport management realities.

## Key Concepts
- AWS CodePipeline, CodeBuild, CodeArtifact integration
- SAP ABAP/NetWeaver transport and change management
- IAM least privilege and environment segregation
- Cryptographic signing with AWS Signer and KMS
- Deployment governance and automated rollback strategies

## Code Example
```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": [
        "codebuild:StartBuild",
        "codebuild:BatchGetBuilds"
      ],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:codebuild:*:*:project/abap-build-*"
    },
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": [
        "codeartifact:PublishPackageVersion",
        "codeartifact:ReadFromRepository"
      ],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:codeartifact:*:*:repository/abap-addons/*"
    },
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": [
        "signer:StartSigningJob",
        "signer:GetSigningProfile"
      ],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:signer:*:*:signing-profile/abap-signing-*"
    }
  ]
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This tests end-to-end observability design for SAP on AWS, tying SAP metrics to AWS cost and performance signals, and validating the candidate's ability to implement a data plane, anomaly detection, and dashboards.

## Key Concepts
- SAP ABAP latency & HANA wait events
- OpenTelemetry + CloudWatch + S3
- SageMaker anomaly detection
- Lambda metric emission & custom metrics
- Cost-aware dashboards (QuickSight)

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal Lambda to emit a CloudWatch metric
const AWS = require('aws-sdk');
const cw = new AWS.CloudWatch();
exports.handler = async () => {
  const latency = await pingSAPAndMeasureLatency();
  await cw.putMetricData({
    Namespace: 'SAP/Observability',
    MetricData: [
      { MetricName: 'ABAP_RPC_Latency_ms', Value: latency, Unit: 'Milliseconds' }
    ]
  }).promise();
};
```

